Only the data is used. Nothing from the repository's scripts (bin/*), from lila or from the
lichess-org/database scripts is copied or run. profile-core::openings::dataset embeds the tables
with include_str!, replays each pgn with chess_core's Position::play_san and keys the final
position by fen_key (EPD: placement, side to move, castling, en-passant square only when a
capture is legal), so a game is classified by the positions it reaches, transpositions included,
not by its move order.

To update: fetch the five files at a new master sha into an empty directory, copy them here,
update the commit, date and checksums above, and run `cargo test -p profile-core --test openings`.
